PASS eta+1 = w(v+w-2)/(w-1)^2
PASS d eta/dv = w/(w-1)^2, a unit everywhere on actual Y
PASS v=u fiber equation eta*w^2+(-2eta-u)*w+(eta+1)=0
PASS at eta=-1 it is w*(2-u-w), with roots 0 and 2-u
PASS discriminant u^2+4eta(u-1), specializing to (u-2)^2
Conclusion: the actual source fiber is smooth but boundary-atypical; one constant puncture escapes to removed w=0.
No relative kernel-surjectivity or monodromy identity is asserted.
